  "consts": [
   "core/parsers/anf_po.py - Abercrombie & Fitch Purchase Order (structural).\n\nLayout (A&F PO, e.g. PO ``3197486-CN3WD-L``):\n\n    Abercrombie & Fitch\n    Purchase Order: 3197486   PO Code: CN3WD-L   Tech Pack: 339260253\n    Commitment: 1190447   Ship Date: 08/28/26   Ship via: AIR - X ...\n    Country of Origin: KH   Carton Std: 6   Currency: USD ...\n    ...\n    PO SKU Summary\n    Bright White 339-293-15126-00316-100-0030 0030 1901... H... 3.75 X SMALL 50\n    ...\n\nOne SKU row carries: colour name + long SKU ``ddd-ddd-ddddd-STYLE-COLOR-SIZECODE``\n+ short SKU + EAN + shade + ticket type + currency + cost + size + qty. The\n``STYLE`` (seg[3]) is the garment style and ``COLOR`` (seg[4]) the colour CODE;\nthe leading words before the long SKU are the human-readable colour NAME.\n\nThe PO references a ``Commitment:`` number but does NOT contain the Key Item\n(KI) / Mill / Fabric - those live in a separate A&F Commitment PDF. After parse,\n``normalize_po`` (or the ANF folder flow) backfills them from the\nCommitmentStore keyed by ``Commitment:``. We store the commitment number in\n``entity.extra[\"commitment_no\"]`` so the join is possible.\n\nEntities are split by ``consolidate_entities_by_style_dest`` on\n``(po_no, style_no, destination_code)``, so a single PO with several styles\nbecomes several entities - exactly the \"one entity per PO+style+destination\"\nrule the user confirmed.\n",
